2026-05-24 23:13:28,479 - INFO - LtM Solve Output 1: Shape-related features generally capture the geometric properties of the silhouettes, which include:

1. Compactness and Circularity: Measure the overall efficiency of the shape concerning area and perimeter/radius relationships (COMPACTNESS, CIRCULARITY, compactness_circularity_ratio).
2. Aspect Ratios: Represent elongation and symmetry properties (RADIUS_RATIO, PR.AXIS_ASPECT_RATIO, MAX.LENGTH_ASPECT_RATIO, SCATTER_RATIO, radius_aspect_ratio_interaction).
3. Rectangularity and Elongatedness: Measure how closely the shape resembles rectangles or line-like forms (ELONGATEDNESS, PR.AXIS_RECTANGULARITY, MAX.LENGTH_RECTANGULARITY).
4. Hollows Ratio: Relates the area of hollows to the bounding polygon (HOLLOWS_RATIO).

Moment-based features capture higher-order characteristics associated with mass distribution and asymmetry:

1. Variances: Measure the spread of the shape along major and minor axes (SCALED_VARIANCE_ALONG_MAJOR_AXIS, SCALED_VARIANCE_ALONG_MINOR_AXIS, major_minor_variance_diff, SCALED_RADIUS_OF_GYRATION).
2. Skewness: Capture asymmetry in mass distribution along axes (SKEWNESS_ABOUT_MAJOR_AXIS, SKEWNESS_ABOUT_MINOR_AXIS).
3. Kurtosis: Highlight extreme outliers or tail properties related to the mass distribution (KURTOSIS_ABOUT_MAJOR_AXIS, KURTOSIS_ABOUT_MINOR_AXIS).
